                <pb facs="0237" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 156.</note>
                <head>Mr. Bancroft to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 126.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation.</hi><hi
                                rendition="#italic"> Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 22, 1870</date>. (Received September
                    7.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The sum of fifty thousand thalers, placed
                    by the royal government at the disposition of our minister at Paris, is designed
                    for the relief, <pb facs="0238" n="204" xml:id="pg204"/> not of Prussians only,
                    but of the poor in Prance of every one of the States of the North German Union.
                    Mr. Washburne is empowered to use it liberally, and has received the assurance
                    that when the first credit is exhausted all further sums that may be necessary
                    will be placed at his disposition. I have great satisfaction in reporting to you
                    that the government is exceedingly well satisfied with the efficient and
                    disinterested manner in which Mr. Washburne discharges his duties. I inclose to
                    you a copy of a letter which I have received from the secretary of state on the
                    subject. I have sent a translation of it to Mr. Washburne.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. BANCROFT.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d156-a1.xml" xpointer="d156-a1"/>
